# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the AM Keramika Next.js application following the latest official Vercel documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Added dependency**: `@vercel/analytics` version `^2.0.1`
- **Package manager**: npm (detected from existing package-lock.json)
- **Files modified**: 
  - `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics to dependencies
  - `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and its dependencies

### 2. Analytics Integration
- **File modified**: `src/app/layout.tsx`
- **Changes**:
  1. Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
  2. Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the body element (after AuthProvider)

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel Analytics Quickstart guide for Next.js App Router:
- Fetched latest documentation from: https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Applied framework-specific instructions for Next.js with App Router
- Placed the Analytics component in the root layout to track all pages
- Component positioned before closing `</body>` tag as recommended

## Build Verification

✅ **Build Status**: Successful
- Ran `npm run build` - completed without errors
- Next.js compiled successfully (Turbopack)
- TypeScript type checking passed
- All 19 routes generated successfully

✅ **Linter**: No new errors introduced
- Ran `npm run lint`
- 2 pre-existing errors in `StorefrontHeader.tsx` (unrelated to this change)
- No errors related to the Analytics integration

## Next Steps for Deployment

After deployment to Vercel, the analytics will:
1. Automatically collect page view data
2. Be accessible via the Vercel project dashboard under "Analytics"
3. Create routes at `/_vercel/insights/*` and `/<unique-path>/*`

To verify functionality after deployment:
- Check browser Network tab for Fetch/XHR requests to `/<unique-path>/view` on page visits
- Access analytics dashboard in Vercel project settings

## Files Changed
- `frontend/package.json` (added dependency)
- `frontend/package-lock.json` (updated lockfile)
- `frontend/src/app/layout.tsx` (added Analytics component)
